  "aciklama": "On April 20, 2010, a blowout destroyed the Deepwater Horizon rig and killed 11 workers. A misread pressure test and a blowout preventer that could not seal the well turned it into the largest marine oil spill in history.\n\nFailure chain: Cement barrier fails → Pressure test misread as pass → Gas rises to the rig → Gas ignites — rig explodes → Bop can't cut buckled pipe\n\nAnother reconstruction: The Disaster That Ended the Age of the Airship — https://youtu.be/PGOKZhPYo7c\n\nFootage & sources:\n• Archival film: \"Deepwater Horizon fire seen by US Coast Guard helicopter\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Deepwater_Horizon_fire_seen_by_US_Coast_Guard_helicopter.ogv\n\nTechnical references:\n• Wikipedia — Deepwater Horizon explosion — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deepwater_Horizon_explosion\n• US Chemical Safety Board — Macondo investigation — https://www.csb.gov/macondo-blowout-and-explosion/\n\nNarration uses a synthetic voice. Footage is real archival film or licensed stock; anything reconstructed is labelled on screen.\n\n#shorts #engineering #industrial",
